From: Jane <jane@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: add Adreno X2-45 (Snapdragon X2 Plus / Mahua)

The Snapdragon X2 Plus (Mahua, e.g. Lenovo Yoga Slim 7 14Q8Y11 / 83QR)
carries an Adreno X2-45. drm/msm reports chip id 0xc144060020 (fuse id
0xc144, core/major/minor 44060020) and the kernel a8xx catalog already
describes it as an A8XX gen2 part with gen80100 firmware, 15.75 MB GMEM
and max_slices = 3, but only 2 slices / 4 CCUs are populated on this SKU.

Mesa 26.3.0 has no entry for it, so both freedreno and turnip refuse to
probe the device:

  fd_pipe_new2:49: unsupported GPU id 0x0 / chip id 0xc144060020
  tu_device.cc:1706: device (chip_id = C144060020, gpu_id = 0) is unsupported

Add the 2-slice A8XX configuration, using the same sub-generation
templates and GPU properties as the X2-85 entry. The 0xffff in bits
47..32 is the fd_dev_info fuse-id wildcard, which makes the exact
chip-id match work for the 0xc144060020 the kernel reports.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
@@ -1589,6 +1589,25 @@
         raw_magic_regs = a8xx_base_raw_magic_regs,
     ))
 
+# 2 slice configuration of Adreno X2-45 (Snapdragon X2 Plus / Mahua)
+add_gpus([
+        GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44060020, name="Adreno (TM) X2-45"),
+    ], A6xxGPUInfo(
+        CHIP.A8XX,
+        [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen3, a8xx_base, a8xx_gen2],
+        num_ccu = 4,
+        num_slices = 2,
+        tile_align_w = 64,
+        tile_align_h = 32,
+        tile_max_w = 16384,
+        tile_max_h = 16384,
+        num_vsc_pipes = 32,
+        cs_shared_mem_size = 32 * 1024,
+        wave_granularity = 2,
+        fibers_per_sp = 64 * 2 * 32,
+        raw_magic_regs = a8xx_base_raw_magic_regs,
+    ))
+
 add_gpus([
         GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44070031, name="Adreno (TM) X2-85"),
         GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44060030, name="Adreno (TM) X2-85"),
